    "done_when": "tests/conftest.py computes a worker's share as max(1, available CPUs // PYTEST_XDIST_WORKER_COUNT), with available CPUs from os.sched_getaffinity(0) where present, and when PYTEST_XDIST_WORKER_COUNT is set it calls pin_thread_pools(share) from a new stdlib-only private module imas_ambix/_thread_pools.py, which sets OMP_NUM_THREADS, OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS and MKL_NUM_THREADS with os.environ.setdefault (an explicit outer setting wins); imas_ambix/statespace/oracle_probe.py calls pin_thread_pools(4) before importing numpy in place of its inline loop; it then calls torch.set_num_threads with the share when torch imports, and limits already-loaded BLAS and OpenMP pools with threadpoolctl.threadpool_limits for the session; without xdist it changes nothing. The comment above it states the mechanism and cites imas_ambix/statespace/oracle_probe.py as the existing pin. A new test file tests/test_worker_threads.py asserts that pin_thread_pools sets the three variables and leaves a preset one unchanged, the share computation on given CPU and worker counts, that nothing is set when PYTEST_XDIST_WORKER_COUNT is absent, and, when the test itself runs under xdist, that torch.get_num_threads() equals the share. On the fleet compute node: UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_worker_threads.py exits 0, and UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 4 tests/test_worker_threads.py exits 0, each into a log with an EXIT line; UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. threadpoolctl is already installed through scikit-learn; its declaration in the dev group is a separate node, so do not edit pyproject.toml or uv.lock. The fragment docs/evidence/fragments/project-environment-declared/ped-worker-threads.html records the share computed for -n 4 and -n 8 on the node and the gate results.",
